<title>GERMANY: German VAW in Chinese foil-making venture.</title>
<headline>German VAW in Chinese foil-making venture.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>VAW Aluminium AG, a unit of the diversified utility Viag AG, said on Monday it was entering into a joint venture with a Chinese company, Jiangsu Daya, to make aluminium foil.</p>
<p>VAW said the two companies had already signed letters of intent. VAW will hold 60 percent of the company and be responsible for its management.</p>
<p>The joint venture will be based in Daya in Jiangsu province and will employ 250 people. The company plans to produce around 4,000 tonnes of aluminium foil annually.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
